<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">What is construction management software?</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
    <strong>Construction management software</strong> is a digital system that replaces spreadsheets, email
    threads, and paper files with one connected platform for planning and running a construction project.
    Instead of tracking budgets in one file, schedules in another, and purchase orders in a third, a
    <strong>project management software for construction</strong> ties everything to shared cost codes so a
    single change — a new purchase order, an updated schedule date, a paid invoice — updates every report
    automatically.
  </p>
  <p class="text-gray-700">
    Most modern platforms are delivered as <strong>construction SaaS</strong> (software as a service): cloud-hosted,
    subscription-based, accessible from a laptop or phone, with no servers to maintain. That shift is why the
    category has grown so quickly — small firms now get capabilities that used to require enterprise IT budgets.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Must-have features in 2026</h2>
  <ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Flexible budgets.</strong> CSI MasterFormat, Uniformat, or custom cost codes so the software matches your standard — not the other way around.</li>
    <li><strong>Schedules with dependencies.</strong> Gantt charts, critical path, and look-aheads that update automatically as work progresses.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchase orders linked to cost codes.</strong> Every commitment tied back to the budget line it draws from.</li>
    <li><strong>Invoice tracking against POs.</strong> So budget-vs-actual is always current, not reconciled once a month.</li>
    <li><strong>One-click reporting.</strong> PDF reports for owners, consultants, and lenders without rebuilding a spreadsheet each time.</li>
    <li><strong>Trade and subcontractor collaboration.</strong> A way for trades to see schedules, update progress, and submit invoices without a separate license fee.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud/mobile access.</strong> Field-usable from a phone or tablet, with no software to install.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">How to choose the right construction software</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
    Enterprise platforms like Procore are built for large general contractors with dedicated administrators.
    Most small and mid-size builders, residential contractors, and trade companies need a narrower — but deeper —
    feature set, at a fraction of the cost. When evaluating options, weigh:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Transparent pricing</strong> — published rates you can budget against, not a custom quote process.</li>
    <li><strong>No per-project fees</strong> — unlimited projects on one subscription.</li>
    <li><strong>Fast onboarding</strong> — a project set up in under an hour, not weeks of training.</li>
    <li><strong>Free or low-cost collaboration</strong> — trades and owners shouldn't cost extra to bring onto a project.</li>
    <li><strong>A real free trial</strong> — enough time to run an actual project through the system before paying.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">
    See our full breakdown in <a href="/procore-alternatives/" class="text-blue-700 underline">Procore alternatives for small &amp; mid-size builders</a>.
  </p>
</section>

